description:
Loads a published GeoZarr collection over a reference period and computes a WMO-style day-of-year climatology (mean per day-of-year, optionally circular-smoothed), then publishes the result as a new GeoZarr dataset with a `dayofyear` dimension (1..366).

Use it to derive normals from a dataset you have already ingested for the reference period — e.g. ingest era5land_temperature_daily for 1991-2020, then compute its day-of-year normal. (To compute normals without ingesting 30 years first, use the `era5land_temperature_normal` / `era5land_precipitation_normal` dataset templates, which read the reference period directly from the Earth Data Hub.)

The `output_dataset_id` must have a registered dataset template on the instance: a YAML in `plugins/datasets/` with `sync: {kind: static}` and a `display` block (colormap/range). No ingestion plugin is required — the data is produced by this workflow.

Zarr output cannot be produced synchronously, so run this as a batch job (`POST /jobs`, then `POST /jobs/{id}/results`):

{
  "normal": {
    "process_id": "climate_normal",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "era5land_temperature_daily",
      "output_dataset_id": "era5land_temperature_normal_from_store",
      "variable": "t2m",
      "temporal_extent": ["1991-01-01", "2020-12-31"],
      "smoothing_window": 31
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
